    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Priya's Music Webpage\r\n_\"I want to make a webpage about my favorite music because I love sharing what I'm listening to with other people. I want each genre to have its own title with the artists listed underneath. The titles should look different from the artist names — maybe a fancier font. And the artist names should be a warm color, like gold or orange._\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/85d3712fe1f9011a73ed96f020d83db6-image-1774473713632.png\" style=\"width: 30%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. Use AI Tutor to build this page step by step. Be specific - name the elements, sizes, colors, and which parts of the page they apply to.\r\n2. Keep prompting until your result is close to Priya's vision. It doesn't need to be identical - just similar enough.\r\n\r\n> **Hint:** Try using `<ul>` and `<h2>` tags in HTML, and the `font-family` and `color` properties in CSS. If you're not sure what some of these are: ask AI Tutor!\r\n\r\nWhen you're satisfied with the result, click **Continue**.",
